NovaPresentationFramework
=========================

This project is MIT-licensed original work. It does not vendor Microsoft
WpfGfx / milcore C++ sources.

It is designed to *consume* upstream `dotnet/wpf` managed assemblies
(PresentationFramework, PresentationCore, WindowsBase, System.Xaml), which
are themselves MIT:

    Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors
    https://github.com/dotnet/wpf/blob/main/LICENSE.TXT

Redistributing those assemblies requires retaining their MIT copyright
notice and LICENSE.TXT. Do not relicense them. Do not copy WpfGfx native
sources into this tree.

Runtime dependencies
--------------------

The runtime loads the third-party libraries described below. Each is
consumed under permissive terms — MIT / Apache-2.0 / zlib / FTL /
Unicode-DFS / MPL. The constraint is structural rather than a preference:
this project redistributes MIT WPF assemblies, so every dependency in the
bundle and in the documented runtime set must stay composable with them in
a single product.

- **SDL3** (zlib) — the windowing and presentation layer (`Nova.Sdl`,
  `Nova.SdlSource`). Ships with the package through `Silk.NET.SDL.Native`
  (`runtimes/linux-x64/native/libSDL3.so`); the consumer never installs it
  separately.
- **Silk.NET Vulkan bindings** (MIT) — the managed binding layer to the
  Vulkan API. No DXVK appears anywhere in the rendering path.
- **Vulkan loader**, `libvulkan.so.1` (Apache-2.0) — resolved by Silk.NET
  at runtime. A system package, never bundled.
- **Mesa lavapipe** (MIT) — the software Vulkan ICD the project tests
  against and documents for CPU/CI runs; it is the same binary as the GPU
  path, selected via `VK_DRIVER_FILES`. A system package, never bundled —
  an ICD must match the driver stack it sits on.
- **HarfBuzz** (MIT, the old-style license text — not the GPL option) —
  text shaping (`Nova.HarfBuzz`).
- **FreeType** (FTL, BSD-like) — glyph raster and font metrics
  (`Nova.FreeType`), consumed under the FTL option, never the GPLv2
  dual-license option.
- **fontconfig** (MIT) — font discovery and matching (`Nova.FontConfig`).
- **ICU**, `libicuuc` (Unicode-DFS) — `Nova.Classification` binds the
  versioned ICU 78 symbols (`u_*_78`). A system package; the same ICU major
  the .NET runtime itself pins.
- **Hunspell** (tri-licensed: LGPL-2.1 / GPL-2 / MPL-1.1) — spell-checking
  (`Nova.Hunspell`), consumed under the **MPL 1.1** option and dynamically
  loaded from the system `libhunspell-1.7` (the Firefox model). Never
  bundled and never statically linked, so MPL file-level copyleft stays
  inside the system library. Loading fails cleanly when the library or a
  dictionary is absent.

Vendored tessellation engine (src/Nova.Geometry2D/Tess/)
---------------------------------------------------------

The sweep-line polygon tessellator under `src/Nova.Geometry2D/Tess/` is
adapted from **LibTessDotNet** (https://github.com/speps/LibTessDotNet)
by Remi Gillig — a C# port of **libtess2** by Mikko Mononen, itself a
port of the **SGI GLU tessellator** by Eric Veach (Silicon Graphics,
July 1994). It is distributed under the **SGI Free Software License B
(Version 2.0, Sept. 18, 2008)**, Copyright (C) 2011 Silicon Graphics, Inc.
All Rights Reserved.

The adaptation is a port/derivative, not an independent reimplementation:
the algorithm, data structures, and the bulk of the code follow
LibTessDotNet line-by-line (modernized to double precision with
span-based contour input, direct triangle output, and a reflection-free
node pool), so the SGI notice obligations apply and are honored. The full
license text is retained in the header of every file under
`src/Nova.Geometry2D/Tess/` (Dict, Geom, Mesh, MeshUtils, PriorityHeap,
PriorityQueue, Sweep, Tess, TessPool, Vec3).

SGI FSL B is a permissive, non-copyleft license with the same rights as
MIT (use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell)
under one condition — the copyright notice must be included in copies or
substantial portions — plus a no-endorsement clause on the SGI name. It is
compatible with shipping in the same product as the MIT-licensed host and
the MIT WPF assemblies; the bundled `Nova.Geometry2D` assembly carries this
code.

Bundled icon font (fonts/NovaFluentIcons.ttf)
---------------------------------------------

The bundled `NovaFluentIcons.ttf` is a derived font used by the Fluent
theme's `SymbolThemeFontFamily` (the theme's default references the
proprietary Segoe Fluent Icons / Segoe MDL2 Assets, which this project does
not redistribute). It is built from:

1. **Uno Fluent Icons** (`uno-fluentui-assets.ttf` from
   https://github.com/unoplatform/uno.fonts), **Apache License 2.0**,
   Copyright (c) nventive / Uno Platform. Uno Fluent Icons is itself an
   assembled work of permissively-licensed glyph sources — **Fluent UI
   System Icons** (MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation), **Line
   Awesome** (MIT / Good Boy License), and **WinJS** (MIT) — whose notices
   are preserved in `fonts/LICENSE-uno-fonts.txt`. Full Apache-2.0 text:
   https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.
2. Two glyphs — `CaretSolidUp` (U+F090) and `CaretSolidDown` (U+F08E), the
   DataGrid sort indicators — merged from **WinSymbols3.ttf** of
   https://github.com/robloo/SymbolIconManager, **MIT License**,
   Copyright (c) 2021 robloo (text in
   `fonts/LICENSE-winsymbols3.txt`).

The font's name table was rewritten to the unique family **"Nova Fluent
Icons"** (the sources' generic family name is "Symbols", which is ambiguous
for fontconfig matching); the two WinSymbols3 glyphs were copied into the
Uno glyph set and mapped to U+F090/U+F08E. Redistribution of the derived
font complies with Apache-2.0 §4 (attribution + license retention, both
provided) and MIT (notice retention). No Segoe font files are bundled.

